    "path": "SKILL.md",
    "content": "---\nname: pinelabs-skills\ndescription: >-\n  Guides Pine Labs Online integration decisions across generated SDKs, raw REST APIs, CLI, MCP,\n  n8n, and agent toolkits. Use when building, modifying, reviewing, testing, or operating any\n  Pine Labs Online payment integration, including checkout, orders, payment links, refunds,\n  settlements, payouts, subscriptions, tokenization, webhooks, or AI-assisted payment workflows.\n---\n\n# Pine Labs Best Practices\n\nPrescriptive guidance for integrating Pine Labs Online payments with APIs, generated SDKs, CLI, MCP, n8n, and agent toolkits.\n\n## Source\n\n- OpenAPI version: `3.0`\n- Spec hash: `sha256:032c753ae331bbdab36e338b3bf3dab5a482380f6029fd72f795f7dd02bdbb24`\n- Generated from: `https://uatcdn.pinelabs.com/pinelabs-docs-online-payments/openapi/v1.yaml`\n\n## Integration Routing\n\n- **Build backend payment integration:** use **Generated SDKs or raw REST API**. Prefer generated SDKs for app code; use raw REST only when an SDK is not available for the stack.\n- **Test, diagnose, reconcile, or operate payments:** use **Pine Labs CLI**. Use CLI profiles, dry runs, UAT first, and explicit production confirmation for money-moving operations.\n- **Connect an AI assistant to Pine Labs APIs:** use **MCP server or agent toolkit**. Use MCP for developer tools and the agent toolkit when embedding Pine Labs tools inside an application agent.\n- **Build no-code workflow automation:** use **n8n node**. Use n8n for payment links, order workflows, notifications, and back-office automations.\n\n## Required Practices\n\n- Default every example and generated integration to UAT: `https://pluraluat.v2.pinepg.in`.\n- Use production only after explicit confirmation: `https://api.pluralpay.in`.\n- Read credentials from `PINELABS_CLIENT_ID` and `PINELABS_CLIENT_SECRET`; never place secrets in browser, mobile, committed code, or logs.\n- Verify webhook signatures before processing any Pine Labs event.\n- For production money-moving operations, require an idempotency key or request ID and record operation, environment, merchant reference, and response identifier.\n- Use MCP UAT at `https://pluralai.v2.pinepg.in/mcp`; use MCP production at `https://mcp.pinelabs.com/mcp` only after live approval.\n\n## Implementation Workflow Guides\n\nRead these workflow guides before API references when the user asks about validation, webhooks, go-live readiness, mistakes, upgrades, or provider migration.\n\n| Workflow | Purpose | Guide |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Validation and Testing | UAT test planning, integration validation, negative cases, and release evidence for Pine Labs payment flows. | [validation-and-testing.md](validation-and-testing.md) |\n| Go Live | Production readiness gates, rollout checklist, and approval safeguards for Pine Labs integrations. | [go-live.md](go-live.md) |\n| Webhooks | Webhook receiver implementation, raw-body handling, signature verification, replay protection, and fulfillment gating. | [webhooks.md](webhooks.md) |\n| Common Mistakes | Frequent Pine Labs integration mistakes and how to prevent unsafe or brittle implementations. | [common-mistakes.md](common-mistakes.md) |\n| Upgrade Advisor | Upgrade installed Pine Labs agent skills, detect stale installs, and explain package/release changes. | [upgrade-advisor.md](upgrade-advisor.md) |\n| Migration Guides | Provider migration routing for moving payment integrations to Pine Labs without copying old provider code. | [migration-guides/README.md](migration-guides/README.md) |\n| Validate Checkout and Orders | UAT coverage for backend order creation, checkout hand-off, idempotency, and final order reconciliation. | [validation-and-testing/checkout-orders.md](validation-and-testing/checkout-orders.md) |\n| Validate Refunds | UAT coverage for full, partial, duplicate, pending, and reconciled refund flows. | [validation-and-testing/refunds.md](validation-and-testing/refunds.md) |\n| Validate Webhooks | Signature, replay, duplicate, ordering, and fulfillment-gate validation for webhook receivers. | [validation-and-testing/webhooks.md](validation-and-testing/webhooks.md) |\n| Validate Mobile and Web SDKs | Callback, app switch, cancellation, interruption, and backend final-state validation for checkout SDKs. | [validation-and-testing/mobile-web-sdks.md](validation-and-testing/mobile-web-sdks.md) |\n| Validate Subscriptions | UAT coverage for plan, subscription, presentation, retry, and lifecycle reconciliation. | [validation-and-testing/subscriptions.md](validation-and-testing/subscriptions.md) |\n| Validate Settlements | UAT reconciliation coverage for payouts, settlements, split settlement, and delayed fund-movement state. | [validation-and-testing/settlements.md](validation-and-testing/settlements.md) |\n| Upgrade Agent Skills Installer | Version-marker, managed-manifest, and local skill catalog upgrade guidance. | [upgrade-advisor/installer.md](upgrade-advisor/installer.md) |\n| Upgrade Pine Labs Integrations | Verified SDK/API/OpenAPI upgrade planning, breaking-change analysis, and regression testing. | [upgrade-advisor/integration.md](upgrade-advisor/integration.md) |\n\n## Domain Routers\n\nUse the domain router first, then the area guidance file, and use the domain reference as an index. For validation, webhook, go-live, troubleshooting, upgrade, or migration asks, read the matching workflow guide before the API reference.\n\n| Domain | Purpose | Router | Area guides | Reference index |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Getting Started | Setup, authentication, environments, and integration kickoff guidance. | [getting-started/README.md](getting-started/README.md) | 2 files in [getting-started/](./getting-started/) | [getting-started/references/REFERENCE.md](getting-started/references/REFERENCE.md) |\n| Payment Gateway | Order lifecycle, checkout, payment methods, customer/token setup, and gateway variants. | [pg/README.md](pg/README.md) | 30 files in [pg/](./pg/) | [pg/references/REFERENCE.md](pg/references/REFERENCE.md) |\n| Settlements | Refunds, payouts, settlement reconciliation, and split settlement workflows. | [settlements/README.md](settlements/README.md) | 4 files in [settlements/](./settlements/) | [settlements/references/REFERENCE.md](settlements/references/REFERENCE.md) |\n| Subscriptions | Plans, recurring subscription lifecycle, and debit presentation/retry flows. | [subscriptions/README.md](subscriptions/README.md) | 3 files in [subscriptions/](./subscriptions/) | [subscriptions/references/REFERENCE.md](subscriptions/references/REFERENCE.md) |\n| P3P | Pine Labs P3P x402, UPI ReservePay, CLI payments, SDK integration, templates, and sandbox guidance. | [p3p/README.md](p3p/README.md) | 2 files in [p3p/](./p3p/) | [p3p/references/REFERENCE.md](p3p/references/REFERENCE.md) |\n\n\n## Production Safety\n\n- Treat `live-money-movement`, `state-changing`, and `sensitive-write` operations as gated actions.\n- In UAT, generate realistic fixtures but avoid real cardholder or customer PII.\n- In production, ask for clear confirmation before create, capture, refund, payout, release, cancel, subscription debit, or tokenization changes.\n- Reuse the same idempotency key when retrying a timed-out state-changing request.\n- Prefer webhooks plus server-side enquiry APIs for final payment state."
