    "path": "validation-and-testing/settlements.md",
    "content": "# Validate Settlements\n\nUse `settlements/README.md` plus the matching payout, settlement, refund, or split-settlement guide for API contracts.\n\n## UAT Scenario Matrix\n\n| Scenario | Expected evidence |\n| Settlement lookup | UTR/reference is mapped to the correct internal ledger record |\n| Payout or release retry | Original request identity is queried before a second money movement |\n| Split release/cancel | Each leg is independently reconciled and idempotent |\n| Delayed settlement | Support view distinguishes pending, failed, and completed state |\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nUse UAT credentials stored server-side, an enabled Pine Labs merchant profile, and the referenced API-area guide before changing an integration.\n\n## Happy Path\n\nExecute the documented backend flow, record the merchant reference and Pine Labs identifiers, and verify final status server-side.\n\n## Failure Path\n\nPreserve the original merchant reference and idempotency key, query the backend state, and present pending, failed, cancelled, and replayed outcomes separately.\n\n## Security Constraints\n\nKeep client secrets, access tokens, card data, OTPs, bank data, and customer PII out of browser/mobile code, prompts, logs, and command arguments.\n\n## Diagnostics\n\nCollect redacted request IDs, merchant references, Pine Labs IDs, webhook IDs, and final backend status before escalating.\n\n## Release Evidence\n\nRecord UAT scenarios, expected and observed status, webhook verification evidence, retry behavior, owner, and rollback decision.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Pine Labs Settlements API](https://www.pinelabs.com/docs/online-payments/api/settlements) (Verified: 2026-08-19)\n- [Pine Labs Refunds API](https://www.pinelabs.com/docs/online-payments/api/refunds) (Verified: 2026-08-19)\n"
