    "path": "p3p/references/REFERENCE.md",
    "content": "# P3P Reference\n\nRouting index for area-specific skill files in this domain.\n\nUse this file to identify the right area file quickly. For full operational detail, read the area file directly.\n\n## API Area Index\n\n| API area | Local guidance file | When to use |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| P3P Pay — UPI ReservePay Payment Skill for AI Agents | `p3p/pay.md` | Use when the user asks to make a payment, charge a client agent, set up UPI ReservePay, create a mandate, or pay using Pine Labs P3P. Also use for questions about Pine Labs P3P as a product — what it is, how it works, x402 protocol, supported payment methods (RESERVE_PAY, OTM, Crypto), mandate lifecycle, token limits, or sandbox setup. Do NOT use for peer-to-peer UPI transfers, general payment-gateway comparisons, or non-P3P integrations. |\n| P3P SDK Integration — x402 Payment Middleware for Applications | `p3p/sdk-integration.md` | Use when a developer asks to integrate Pine Labs P3P payments into an application, set up x402 payment middleware, protect an API route with a 402 challenge, handle 402 responses automatically in a client app, or install and configure p3p-server-sdk, p3p-client-sdk, pinelabs-online-p3p-server-sdk, or pinelabs-online-p3p-client-sdk. Covers TypeScript (Next.js, Express, Vanilla JS) and Python (Flask, FastAPI). Do NOT use for CLI-driven agent payments (use p3p-pay skill instead) or non-P3P payment integrations. |\n\n## P3P Resource Files\n\nUse these deeper resources only after selecting the P3P pay or SDK integration skill.\n\n| Resource type | Local path |\n| --- | --- |\n| CLI references | `p3p/references/cli-setup.md`, `p3p/references/cli-mandates.md`, `p3p/references/cli-tokens.md`, `p3p/references/cli-debit.md` |\n| SDK references | `p3p/references/integration-flow.md`, `p3p/references/server-sdk-api-reference.md`, `p3p/references/client-sdk-api-reference.md`, `p3p/references/test-data.md` |\n| SDK templates | `p3p/templates/nextjs/`, `p3p/templates/express/`, `p3p/templates/python/`, `p3p/templates/vanilla/` |\n| Evals | `p3p/evals/p3p-pay.evals.json` |\n\n## Usage Pattern\n\n1. Start with the domain router file.\n2. Open the matching area guidance file for implementation details.\n3. Re-check root safety rules before production changes.\n"
